  "verbalization": "Ammonia is implicated in the pathogenesis of Psoriasis through a series of indirect but interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Ammonia may act as a precursor or modulator in the treatment of Psoriasis, as it is linked to conditions such as Pityriasis Simplex, Acne, and Seborrheic Keratosis, all of which are associated with the skin condition Psoriasis. The presence of Allantoin, a compound that is indicated for Psoriasis, further supports a potential role for Ammonia in the therapeutic context of Psoriasis, as Allantoin is known to have anti-inflammatory properties. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Ammonia influences the skin condition, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be elucidated. The evidence suggests a potential dependency on Ammonia for the treatment of Psoriasis, but the precise mechanism requires further investigation."
